{% comment %}
  Therapy flow — Step 2 of 2, "Therapy Details" (node 543:1462). Reached
  from the therapy Confirm/Continue button on Step 1 of 2 (see
  kal-booking-flow-step-therapy-slot.liquid and kal-booking-flow.js's
  therapyFlowState) once it's in "continue" mode.

  Same shape as the consultation flow's Patient Details step (name,
  gender, phone, email) — reuses that step's exact data attributes
  (data-kal-field="name"/"whatsapp"/"email", data-kal-gender,
  data-kal-patient-continue) so it shares the SAME patientDetails state
  and isPatientDetailsValid()/updatePatientContinueButton() validation in
  kal-booking-flow.js with zero new JS needed for the form itself — one
  visit's details, collected once, regardless of which flow got here.
  Field ids are still unique per step (kal-therapy-patient-* vs
  kal-patient-*) since both steps' markup sits in the DOM at once (only
  one is unhidden) and duplicate ids would break label-click focusing.

  Gender is Male/Female only, matching Patient Details' own explicit
  instruction (the Figma export for THIS node also showed a third
  "Other" pill — dropped for the same reason, same instruction reused
  here: "for now maintain only male and female").

  The appointment card here is NOT the shared kal-booking-flow-appointment-
  card.liquid — that one shows a mode+price row, but this node's card
  shows degree/experience badges (reusing Doctor Select's doctor-education/
  doctor-experience icons) and a description line about the therapy
  starting with a short doctor consultation. Different enough content
  shape that duplicating the shared card's photo+name structure inline
  here (as .kal-therapy-appointment-card) was simpler than adding
  optional/conditional slots to the shared one for a single caller.

  Footer button is "Submit Request", not "Continue" — matches this node's
  own export. It navigates to the new "therapy-confirmed" step (node
  539:2222, the therapy flow's own success screen) once the form is
  valid — a plain data-kal-goto is safe here (unlike Step 1 of 2's own
  Confirm/Continue button) since this button has no separate "confirm
  first" stage; it's just disabled until isPatientDetailsValid().
{% endcomment %}

<div class="kal-step-therapy-details kal-step-shell kal-step-shell--progress-panel">

  {%- comment -%}
    Desktop left column — same pattern as therapy-slot.liquid's own left
    column (see that file's comment) — current_step: 2 now, so "Choose
    therapy" reads Completed and "Personal details" reads In progress.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="kal-step-entry__info kal-step-shell__info kal-concern-select__info">
    <div class="kal-concern-select__info-scroll">
      <div class="kal-concern-select__info-header">
        <h2 class="kal-step-entry__heading kal-concern-select__heading">Therapy Request</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-concern-select__info-section">
        <p class="kal-concern-select__info-label">Selected Clinic</p>
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-facility-picker', step_number: 2, location_text: 'Indiranagar', extra_class: 'kal-concern-select__info-pill' -%}
      </div>

      {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-step-progress', current_step: 2, step_names: 'Choose therapy|Personal details' -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kal-step-shell__panel">

    {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-step-header', back_target: 'therapy-slot', step_number: 2, step_total: 2, next_label: 'Final step' -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Heading + therapy/doctor summary card moved OUTSIDE
      .kal-step-shell__scroll (still siblings within .kal-step-shell__panel)
      per explicit instruction — only the form fields should scroll, with
      these staying fixed right below the progress bar, same treatment as
      Concern Select's own heading/banner.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__intro">
      <h2 class="kal-step-doctor-select__heading">Enter your patient details</h2>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Photo removed per explicit instruction (flow-wide) — plain
      placeholder box instead of the doctor's photo for now.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="kal-therapy-appointment-card">
      <div class="kal-therapy-appointment-card__top">
        <span class="kal-therapy-appointment-card__photo">
          <span class="kal-doctor-photo-placeholder"></span>
        </span>
        <span class="kal-therapy-appointment-card__body">
          <span class="kal-therapy-appointment-card__name">Dr. Neethu Jayachandran</span>
          <span class="kal-therapy-appointment-card__meta">
            <span class="kal-therapy-appointment-card__meta-item">
              <span class="kal-therapy-appointment-card__meta-icon">
                {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'doctor-education' -%}
              </span>
              BAMS
            </span>
            <span class="kal-therapy-appointment-card__divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="kal-therapy-appointment-card__meta-item">
              <span class="kal-therapy-appointment-card__meta-icon">
                {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'doctor-experience' -%}
              </span>
              12 yrs experience
            </span>
          </span>
        </span>
      </div>
      <span class="kal-therapy-appointment-card__desc">
        Your therapy starts with a short <strong>doctor consultation</strong> and is performed by an expert therapist.
      </span>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-shell__scroll">
      <div class="kal-form">
        <div class="kal-form-field">
          <label class="kal-form-label" for="kal-therapy-patient-name">Full name*</label>
          <input
            type="text"
            id="kal-therapy-patient-name"
            class="kal-form-input"
            data-kal-field="name"
            placeholder="Enter full name"
            autocomplete="name"
          >
        </div>

        <div class="kal-form-field">
          <p class="kal-form-label">Gender*</p>
          <div class="kal-gender-group" data-kal-gender-group>
            <button type="button" class="kal-gender-btn" data-kal-gender="female">Female</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-gender-btn" data-kal-gender="male">Male</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="kal-form-row">
          <div class="kal-form-field">
            <label class="kal-form-label" for="kal-therapy-patient-whatsapp">Phone Number*</label>
            {%- comment -%}
              Country-code chip is decorative — same "visual match, not
              wired" treatment as Patient Details' own copy of this.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="kal-phone-input">
              <span class="kal-phone-input__country" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="kal-phone-input__flag">
                  <span class="kal-phone-input__flag-stripe kal-phone-input__flag-stripe--saffron"></span>
                  <span class="kal-phone-input__flag-stripe kal-phone-input__flag-stripe--white"></span>
                  <span class="kal-phone-input__flag-stripe kal-phone-input__flag-stripe--green"></span>
                </span>
                <span class="kal-phone-input__code">+91</span>
                <span class="kal-phone-input__chevron">
                  {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'chevron-down' -%}
                </span>
              </span>
              <input
                type="tel"
                id="kal-therapy-patient-whatsapp"
                class="kal-form-input kal-phone-input__field"
                data-kal-field="whatsapp"
                placeholder="10-digit mobile number"
                autocomplete="tel"
                inputmode="numeric"
              >
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="kal-form-field">
            <label class="kal-form-label" for="kal-therapy-patient-email">
              Email <span class="kal-form-label__optional">Optional</span>
            </label>
            <input
              type="email"
              id="kal-therapy-patient-email"
              class="kal-form-input"
              data-kal-field="email"
              placeholder="Enter email address"
              autocomplete="email"
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-shell__footer kal-concern-select__footer kal-concern-select__footer--mobile">
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue" data-kal-goto="therapy-confirmed" data-kal-patient-continue disabled>
        Submit Request
      </button>
    </div>

  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Desktop-only full-width footer bar, same pattern as the consultation
    flow's progress-panel steps — help text + Back (to Therapy Slot)/
    Submit Request split across the shared 300px/1fr grid columns.
    data-kal-goto="therapy-confirmed" + data-kal-patient-continue on this
    button work the exact same way as the mobile instance (see
    kal-booking-flow.js's patientContinueTrigger handler, which now
    reads a button's own data-kal-goto instead of always hardcoding
    'confirmation' — fixed specifically so this shared hook works
    correctly for both flows).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="kal-step-shell__footer kal-concern-select__footer kal-concern-select__footer--desktop">
    <div class="kal-concern-select__footer-help kal-step-entry__help">
      <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--help">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'help-circle' -%}
      </span>
      <span class="kal-step-entry__help-text">Need assistance? Call us at +91 804012 3456</span>
    </div>
    <div class="kal-concern-select__footer-actions">
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__back kal-concern-select__footer-back" data-kal-back="therapy-slot" aria-label="Back">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'chevron-left' -%}
        <span>Back</span>
      </button>
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue" data-kal-goto="therapy-confirmed" data-kal-patient-continue disabled>
        Submit Request
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>
